From: apklayer <apklayer@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] apklayer patch: exclusive-monitor epochs (LDXR/STXR no longer ABA-unsafe)

LDXR/STXR were a compare-and-swap of the loaded value: an ABA sequence (pop, pop, push of the same node on an untagged LL/SC free list) let a stale STXR succeed, which arm64 forbids (any store to the reserved granule clears the monitor). A 16 KB table of counters below 2 GB (runtime_primitives/exclusive_epoch.h, indexed by address bits 4..13, each entry a 32-bit counter and a 64-bit lock word): LDXR reads its counter before the value and keeps it in the upper half of cpu.reservation_value; STXR takes the entry lock, fails when the counter moved, does the compare-and-swap, bumps the counter and unlocks (also on a fault). Interpreter and lite tier; the heavy tier bails on LDXR/STXR so such regions stay lite-translated. LDXP/STXP unchanged. Module libberberis_arm64. Tested: tests/apps/hello-arm64/locks.c llsc64 phase (1.1 million lost nodes before, 0 after).
